+- Status: superseded. The maintainer explicitly overrode this decision on 2026-10-23.
+- Decision (old): `set -uo pipefail` without `-e`. Every internal error still ends in `exit 0`; the script only warns.
+- Forbidden (old): `set -e` or `set -o errexit`, and any exit status other than 0.
+- Reason (old): with `set -e`, a `wc` failure on a staged-then-deleted file aborted the check and blocked every commit in
   the repository for a day (2026-09-10). The check is advisory by design.
+
+### §check-aborts-on-failure — any failing command aborts the check with a non-zero exit
+- Since: 2026-10-23
+- Supersedes: §check-fails-open (the user/maintainer overrode it explicitly, naming that decision).
+- Decision: `set -euo pipefail` (plus `shopt -s inherit_errexit` where supported). Any failing command aborts the check
+  with a non-zero exit. Finding large staged files still only warns and ends in `exit 0`.
+- Known risk: the 2026-09-10 incident (a `wc` failure on a staged-then-deleted file blocking commits) is the failure
+  mode this accepts; the loop skips non-existent files via `[ -f "$f" ] || continue` to limit it.
